<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="MIPS:LE:32:default:default">
<!--
    kuna: a register a MIPS function sets for coprocessor 0 is not the high
    word of its return; a prefetch, cache op or coprocessor 2 move of it is
    no such write.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 return recovery, the output trials of the
    function's own RETURN (ActionReturnRecovery, p4_calls/kuna_retsysreg.rs).
    P0 assertion: option retsysreg on|off (default on).

    Source (mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc -O2, bytes verbatim; 0x1000 and 0x1100):

        typedef unsigned int u32; typedef unsigned long long u64;
        u64 pk(u32 *p) { u32 q = p[1]; __builtin_prefetch((void*)q);
          return ((u64)q << 32) | p[0]; }
        u64 pkw(u32 *p, u32 n) { u32 q = p[n]; __builtin_prefetch((void*)q, 1);
          return ((u64)q << 32) | p[0]; }
        cch, syn, cop2: pk with cache 0x15,0(q), synci 0(q) and mtc2 q,$1
        int st(int a) { int r = a * 3; register int v asm("$3") = 0x1001;
          __asm volatile("mtc0 %0, $12" :: "r"(v)); return r; }

    pk is lw v1,4(a0); lw v0,0(a0); jr ra; pref 6,0(v1).
    st is sll v0,a0,1; li v1,0x1001; addu v0,v0,a0; jr ra; mtc0 v1,$12.

    The bug: v1 joined v0 as a 64-bit return whose high word is the Status
    operand.  The fix returns the 32-bit value from st.  pk, pkw, cch, syn
    and cop2 keep the pair: a prefetch or cache op takes an address, which
    the high word can be, and coprocessor 2 takes data.  The last pass sets
    option retsysreg off and prints st with the pair again.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000" readonly="true">
0400838c0000828c0800e003000066cc802805000000828c212885000000a38c
0800e003000067cc
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1100" readonly="true">
0400838c000075bc0800e0030000828c0400838c00007f040800e0030000828c
0400838c000883480800e0030000828c0400838c001083440800e0030000828c
4010040001100324211044000800e00300608340
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="pk"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1010" name="pkw"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1100" name="cch"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1110" name="syn"/>
